      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: \n\nThe GrabPass issue (can't use it in VR on Quest) is a bug in Unity. (Fixed in 2021) https://issuetracker.unity3d.com/issues/oculus-go-oculus-quest-using-grabpass-results-incorrect-shader-rendering-when-using-single-pass-stereo-rendering\n\nThe Geometry shader and the Tessellation are hardware restriction that these aren't usable during multiview.\n\nThe MultiView function is used for rendering VR on Quest.\n\nhttp://vulkan.gpuinfo.org/displayreport.php?id=10024#features_extensions\n\nmultiviewGeometryShader and multiviewTessellationShader on this page must be true to be usable in VR.\n\nI think all of these works correctly on non-VR cameras even on Quest.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-24T22:45:56.440Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Shaders behave differently in non-VR and VR.\n\nTherefore, Quest and VRHMD are always needed to test shaders.\n\nIf Desktop/Mobile clients can use MockHMD, we can test shaders without VRHMD and Quest.\n\nThis is important for the Quest/Mobile environment because some shader functions(GrabPass, Geometry shader, Tessellation) work well on mobile, but not on Quest (VR).",
